{"name":"Valentine’s Kiss","hex":"#b63364","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"valentine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An expression of affection, especially romantic affection, usually in the form of greeting card, gift, or message given the object of one's affection, especially on February 14th.","A person to whom a valentine is given or from whom it is received, especially on February 14th."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valentine"},{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Valentine Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"\"Valentine Kiss\"  is the solo debut J-pop single from Sayuri Kokushō released on February 1, 1986, by CBS Sony in Japan. Kokushō was the eighth member of Onyanko Club. The B-side song was \"Koi wa Ring Ring Ring\" ."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/Valentine_Kiss_by_Sayuri_Kokusho.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentine_Kiss"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/11/Watariroukahashiritai7v.jpg/250px-Watariroukahashiritai7v.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/11/Watariroukahashiritai7v.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/11/Watariroukahashiritai7v.jpg/250px-Watariroukahashiritai7v.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWatariroukahashiritai7v.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/500px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/1280px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/500px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A forehead kiss","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSMC-16853.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/US_Navy_060105-N-3019M-002_Boatswain%27s_Mate_3rd_Class_Leroy_Quinn_kisses_his_son_on_the_pier_before_departing_aboard_the_guided_missile_destroyer_USS_Chung-Hoon_%28DDG_93%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail